  "query_preview": "the Heat Advisory for the northwestern portion (along and\nnorth of a Sumter-Shelby-Cherokee County line) through 9 pm\nWednesday.\n\nThe center of the big upper ridge responsible for the enhanced\nheat/humidity combo is forecast to push northeastward over the\ncoming days, which will put us on the south side of the bubble.\nA tropical easterly flow, and a slight weakening of the subsidence\nassociated with the upper high, will allow for diurnal\nthunderstorm development through the rest of the week. Best rain\nchances each day will largely be determined by mesoscale\ninfluences (previous days' leftover boundaries, cloudy/clear\nboundaries, elevated heat sources, etc.). POPs in the 20-30\npercent range seem reasonable. As the ridge further breaks down\nover the weekend and early next week, then POPs are likely to inch\nup a bit more.\n\n/61/",
